  }
}
== claude/CLAUDE.md
<!-- mi6 layer: $EXAMPLES/home/.mi6 -->

# This machine

This machine runs local models through LM Studio on port 1234.

<!-- mi6 layer: $EXAMPLES/tree/.mi6 -->

# Every repo in this tree

- Commit messages: a concise subject line and a body that says why.
- Never commit secrets. Source them from a gitignored file.
- Repo and directory names use kebab-case.
- A deny rule here reaches every repo below and no layer can lift it, so
  keep this list short.

<!-- mi6 layer: $EXAMPLES/tree/work/.mi6 -->

# Work

Projects for the employer. Use the work GitHub account for anything pushed.

<!-- mi6 layer: $EXAMPLES/tree/work/clients/.mi6 -->

# Client work

These repos belong to clients. Never add agent config files to the repo.
Never push. Prepare commits and stop.

<!-- mi6 layer: $EXAMPLES/tree/work/clients/globex/.mi6 -->

# Globex

Globex runs everything in one monorepo. The pipelines are under `dags/`.
Their style guide is at `docs/style.md` in the repo.
== claude/settings.json
{
  "availableModels": [
    "sonnet",
    "haiku"
  ],
  "enforceAvailableModels": true,
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(git status)",
      "Bash(git diff *)",
      "Bash(git log *)",
      "Bash(make *)",
      "Bash(docker compose *)"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Read(~/.ssh/**)",
      "Bash(git push *)"
    ]
  }
}
